<title>USA: Connecticut Treasurer Burnham resigns.</title>
<headline>Connecticut Treasurer Burnham resigns.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Connecticut Treasurer Christopher Burnham (R) said Thursday he will resign at the end of this summer to join an investment firm in Stamford, Connecticut.</p>
<p>Burnham, 40, told a news conference he will become president and chief executive officer of Columbus Circle Investors.</p>
<p>Burnham said he had accomplished all he had set out to when he was elected in 1994 as the first Republican to hold the office in a generation.</p>
<p>Prior to becoming state treasurer, Burnham was a corporate finance banker in New York City and Hartford.</p>
<p>((Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224))</p>
